    answer: 'A WodeMac cloud Mac is delivered with the WodeMac Remote Screen app, which opens the full desktop from a computer, phone or iPad, and WodeMac helps you with the first login. SSH (Remote Login) and Screen Sharing are built-in macOS features, not connection methods promised at delivery. With admin rights you can turn them on in System Settings if you need them, after confirming they can be reached from your network. For everyday work the remote screen is enough; consider SSH when most of your work is in a terminal.',
